WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.630
Physical weathering breaks rock apart without requiring a change in its

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:09.090
minerals. Near-surface fracturing can accompany unloading or a fall from a

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.750
cliff. Freezing water and growing salt crystals widen cracks.

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.670
Roots can pry fractures apart, while burrowing exposes material.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.690
Thermal expansion can contribute, but this textbook explicitly qualifies its relative

00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.170
importance.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.470
Chemical weathering changes or removes minerals.

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:28.230
Dissolution puts soluble components into water.

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.410
Oxidation forms oxides, including reddish iron oxides.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:37.370
Hydrolysis reacts water with silicate minerals and commonly produces clay plus

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:42.030
dissolved material. Acids and other biological reactions can also break minerals

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:45.610
down. These are chemical changes, not simply the rounding of a

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:45.830
stone.

00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:51.370
Starting composition matters. Soluble limestone can develop pits and grooves as

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:55.670
water removes material. In granite, feldspar may alter to clay or

00:00:55.670 --> 00:01:00.070
survive as grains, resistant quartz commonly remains as sand, and dark

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.490
minerals can yield clay and iron oxides.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.930
One original rock can therefore supply several sediment sizes and compositions.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.490
Fracturing makes a rock weaker and increases the surface available to

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:16.850
water, air and organisms. Physical breakup can accelerate chemical reactions, and

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.510
chemical alteration can weaken rock for further breakup.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:23.330
Highly fractured parts of a unit may erode into notches or

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:27.250
lower terrain. The two forms of weathering often reinforce each other.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:32.350
After weathering loosens material, streams, waves, wind, ice and gravity can

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:36.750
move it. Collisions break clasts, and abrasion scrapes surfaces and rounds

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.010
exposed corners. Moving sediment can also scour bedrock and create more

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:43.010
fragments. Keep the steps distinct:

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:47.430
weathering produces loose or dissolved material, erosion removes it, and transport

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:48.350
carries it elsewhere.
